Current Data Status

The current repository contains a development/test dataset designed to validate the analytical pipeline.

It should not be interpreted as an official UK national-accounts dataset.

The next research stage is to replace the development data with official UK macroeconomic data from sources such as:

UK Office for National Statistics
Bank of England

The model architecture is designed so that the analytical pipeline can be rerun after replacing the raw dataset.

Methodological Considerations

Several methodological issues are deliberately incorporated into the project.

GDP Identity

Official national accounts may contain statistical discrepancies, and expenditure components may not sum exactly to published GDP depending on the measurement framework.

The model therefore reports the identity residual rather than silently forcing the identity to balance.

Econometrics

The current test dataset is too small for reliable causal inference.

Regression results should therefore be regarded as exploratory.

Forecasting

The scenario model is based on expenditure-component assumptions and is intended for scenario analysis rather than a fully specified structural macroeconomic forecast.

Data Revisions

Official national-account statistics can be revised.

A production version should therefore record:

Data vintage
Publication date
Source
Frequency
Units
Seasonal-adjustment status
Real/nominal classification
